{%- comment -%}
  The product card's type line — "TYPE • size • size". The type is a label;
  the sizes after it are the product's variants, and each one is a control:
  picking it points the card's add-to-cart at that variant and re-prices the
  card. Without JS each is still a link to the product page with that variant
  preselected, so the line does something useful either way.

  A single-variant product has nothing to choose between, so it shows its type
  alone rather than a lone chip that cannot be unpicked.

  Both cards in the theme render this: the stock card-product snippet and the
  Browse By Concern section's own card. It is one snippet so the line cannot
  say one thing in a collection grid and another on the home page.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} the product to describe

  Usage:
  {% render 'product-card-meta', product: product %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign selected = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign show_variants = false
  if product.variants.size > 1
    assign show_variants = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if product.type != blank or show_variants -%}
  <p class="card__meta" data-soldout-label="{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t | escape }}">
    {%- if product.type != blank -%}
      <span class="card__meta-item">{{ product.type }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_variants -%}
      {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
        {%- if forloop.first == false or product.type != blank -%}
          <span class="card__meta-sep" aria-hidden="true">•</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        <a
          class="card__variant{% if variant.id == selected.id %} is-selected{% endif %}{% unless variant.available %} is-unavailable{% endunless %}"
          href="{{ product.url }}?variant={{ variant.id }}"
          data-card-variant
          data-variant-id="{{ variant.id }}"
          data-variant-price="{{ variant.price | money }}"
          data-variant-compare="{% if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price %}{{ variant.compare_at_price | money }}{% endif %}"
          data-variant-available="{{ variant.available }}"
          aria-pressed="{% if variant.id == selected.id %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
        >
          {{- variant.title -}}
        </a>
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
